LiteRT 2.3.2 (tflite/): saturate the int16 steps of the NEON int8 / uint8 ADD, SUB and MUL kernels

The optimised NEON kernels narrow the rescaled 32-bit result to 16 bits and then add the output
zero point in 16 bits. ADD / SUB narrow without saturation (vmovn_s32) and all of them add without
saturation (vaddq_s16), so a result beyond the int16 range wraps around and the output takes the
opposite extreme: an int8 MUL with a requantisation multiplier of about 4 gives 127 where it must
give -128 (checked on the NPU die with the built-in kernels, XNNPACK off; the reference kernels and
XNNPACK are right). Saturating narrowing (vqmovn_s32) and saturating addition (vqaddq_s16) give the
result of the reference kernels.


